```typescript
// New logic:
function formatPriceDisplay(pricing?: PricingTier[] | null): string | null {
  if (!pricing || pricing.length === 0) return null;

  if (pricing.length === 1) {
    return `¥${pricing[0].amount.toLocaleString()}`;
  }

  // Multiple tiers: show range (min - max)
  const amounts = pricing.map((p) => p.amount);
  const min = Math.min(...amounts);
  const max = Math.max(...amounts);

  if (min === max) {
    return `¥${min.toLocaleString()}`;
  }
  return `¥${min.toLocaleString()} ~ ¥${max.toLocaleString()}`;
}
```

This function can be defined inline in EventListItem.tsx or extracted to a utility if reused. Given the project convention of keeping page-specific logic co-located, keeping it in-file is appropriate.

The component renders this at line 94 where `priceOrCondition` is currently displayed. The `event.description` dependency is completely removed.

**Decision on "free" events:** If `pricing` is empty/null, we show nothing (no price line). If the admin wants to indicate free events, they can add a pricing tier with amount 0 and label like "フリーカンパ" or similar. This is more explicit than the current hack of searching description text.

